{"message":"Success","data":{"uuid":"N2732835","newswiz_id":"2732835","published_at":1795255464,"tags":[{"id":2,"name":"Reports and Surveys","is_followed":false,"is_notify":false}],"main_tag":{"id":2,"name":"Reports and Surveys","is_followed":false,"is_notify":false},"category":{"id":1,"name":"General","is_main":1,"is_followed":false,"is_notify":false},"country":null,"city":null,"default_image_url":null,"locale":"en","title":"Seasonal Rains Boost Sorghum Cultivation Across Aseer Plains","subtitle":null,"content":"Abha, November 21, 2026, SPA -- The plains and valleys of Tihama in Aseer Region are witnessing peak agricultural activity as vast stretches of fields turn vibrant green with maturing sorghum crops preparing for the early green-grain phase and subsequent full harvest.\nThis agricultural flourishing is driven by moderate temperatures coinciding with seasonal rains that saturate the soil, alongside nutrient-rich floodwaters descending from the Sarawat highlands that are captured within traditional earthen irrigation basins to replenish soil fertility.\nLocal farmers and residents eagerly anticipate the early harvest phase, when soft, immature green grains are gathered and easily ground into key ingredients for traditional dishes. Serving as a vital economic resource, both fresh green grains and fully ripened crops are sold in local markets, while the green stalks and leaves provide high-value fodder for livestock breeders, supporting food security and sustainable rural development.\n-- SPA\r\n13:04 Local Time 10:04 GMT\r\n0018","hashtags":[],"royal_news_types":[],"date_hijri":"1448-06-11","is_report":true,"related_news":[],"parent_news":null,"report_tasks":[],"translations":[{"uuid":"N2732806","locale":"ar"},{"uuid":"N2732874","locale":"fr"},{"uuid":"N2733970","locale":"ru"}],"media_images":{"attachment_display":1,"files":[{"id":4606813,"file":{"id":4677991,"uuid":"M11285086","path":"https://portalcdn.spa.gov.sa/backend/original/202611/M11285086.jpg","sizes":